\title{llmsa: Measurement System Analysis for Pipelines Built on Large Language Models}
\description{
Treats a pipeline built on a large language model (LLM) as a measurement system and validates it with the tools that analytical laboratories already use: crossed precision studies with variance components (gauge repeatability and reproducibility), attribute agreement with kappa statistics, bias against a reference, Plackett-Burman screening of robustness against prompt and formatting perturbations, simulation-based planning of study size, Westgard-rule control charts for ongoing system suitability, and a reproducible validation report. The package is pipeline-agnostic: any backend that turns a prompt and a model identifier into a text response can be validated, and results produced elsewhere can be imported.
